{"builder":"Goal: one pull request on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test that makes packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js lint several files (and stdin via -) and meets every acceptance line of https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/104:\n1. packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> [<file> ...] checks every file named in order and prints <file>:<line>: <error> for each bad row, as for one file before\n2. A file named - is read from stdin and reported as -; a second - is a usage error (exit 2)\n3. Exit 0 if every file is clean, 1 if any row in any file is bad, 2 if no file is named or any file can't be read (error on stderr, other files still checked and reported)\n4. lint(text) in src/index.js is unchanged\n5. node:test tests cover two clean files, one bad among several, stdin via - (clean and bad), a missing file among good ones, two - arguments and no arguments; the package README documents the usage\n6. The change is one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body says Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/104, and npm test and the test workflow are green at its head\n\nSteps:\n1. Read packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js, packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js, packages/jsonl-lint/test/cli.test.js, packages/jsonl-lint/test/lint.test.js and packages/jsonl-lint/README.md. Today the CLI reads only process.argv[2].\n2. Do not touch packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js at all (not even whitespace); all changes go in the bin, tests and README.\n3. Rewrite the CLI over process.argv.slice(2):\n   - No arguments: print a usage line (e.g. `usage: jsonl-lint <file> [<file> ...]`) to stderr, exit 2.\n   - More than one `-` argument: usage error on stderr, exit 2. Decide this before reading anything (do not consume stdin first).\n   - Otherwise process the arguments in the order given. For `-` read stdin in full (e.g. readFileSync(0, 'utf8')) and use the literal name `-` as the prefix; for others readFileSync(file, 'utf8') and use the argument exactly as given as the prefix.\n   - For each bad row print `<name>:<line>: <error>` on stdout exactly as the single-file version did (same newline-to-space replacement on the error), so output for several files equals the concatenation of single-file runs.\n   - If a file cannot be read, write `jsonl-lint: cannot read <file>: <message>` to stderr and continue with the remaining files (do not exit early).\n   - Final exit code: 2 if any file could not be read; else 1 if any bad row was found; else 0.\n4. Extend packages/jsonl-lint/test/cli.test.js (node:test, spawnSync the bin; pass stdin with the `input` option) with tests for: two clean files (exit 0, no output); one bad file among several clean ones (exit 1, only that file's lines, in order with its name as prefix); stdin via `-` clean (exit 0) and bad (exit 1, lines prefixed `-:`); a missing file among good ones (exit 2, stderr names the missing file, and a bad file named after the missing one is still reported on stdout); two `-` arguments (exit 2, stderr non-empty); no arguments (exit 2, stderr non-empty). Keep the existing tests passing.\n5. Update packages/jsonl-lint/README.md: usage `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> [<file> ...]`, that `-` reads stdin and is reported as `-` and may appear only once, that files are checked in order, and the exit codes 0/1/2 as in line 3 (unreadable files reported on stderr while the others are still checked).\n6. Run `npm test` at the repository root; it must pass. Also try the CLI by hand with several files, `-`, `- -`, no args and a missing file.\n7. Commit, push, and open one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body contains the line `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/104`. Wait for the `test` workflow (.github/workflows/test.yml) to finish at the PR head and fix anything red with further commits on the same PR.","verifier":"Check out the PR head and run every command below from the repository root. Each check is for one expect line of https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/104, in order. Commands create their own temp files; $T in outputs is the temp dir.\n\nCheck 1 — expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> [<file> ...] checks every file named in order and prints <file>:<line>: <error> for each bad row, as for one file before\"\nRun:\nT=$(mktemp -d) && printf '{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b\":2}\\n' > \"$T/good1.jsonl\" && printf '[1]\\n' > \"$T/good2.jsonl\" && printf '{\"a\":1}\\n{oops}\\n\\n{\"c\":\\n' > \"$T/bad.jsonl\" && printf '{bad\\n' > \"$T/bad2.jsonl\" && B=packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js && node \"$B\" \"$T/good1.jsonl\" \"$T/bad.jsonl\" \"$T/good2.jsonl\" \"$T/bad2.jsonl\" > \"$T/multi.out\"; echo \"exit=$?\"; for f in good1 bad good2 bad2; do node \"$B\" \"$T/$f.jsonl\"; done > \"$T/single.out\"; cat \"$T/multi.out\"; diff \"$T/single.out\" \"$T/multi.out\" && echo SAME\nPASS: stdout shows exactly three lines in this order: `$T/bad.jsonl:2: <error>`, `$T/bad.jsonl:4: <error>`, `$T/bad2.jsonl:1: <error>` (each <error> non-empty), and the run ends with `SAME` (multi-file output equals the concatenation of single-file runs). FAIL: any of those lines missing, out of order, extra lines, wrong prefix, or no `SAME`.\n\nCheck 2 — expect: \"A file named - is read from stdin and reported as -; a second - is a usage error (exit 2)\"\nRun:\nT=$(mktemp -d) && printf '{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b\":2}\\n' > \"$T/good1.jsonl\" && printf '[1]\\n' > \"$T/good2.jsonl\" && printf '{\"a\":1}\\n{oops}\\n\\n{\"c\":\\n' > \"$T/bad.jsonl\" && printf '{bad\\n' > \"$T/bad2.jsonl\" && B=packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js && echo '--- A: bad via stdin'; node \"$B\" - < \"$T/bad.jsonl\"; echo \"exit=$?\"; echo '--- B: clean stdin with a file'; node \"$B\" \"$T/good2.jsonl\" - < \"$T/good1.jsonl\"; echo \"exit=$?\"; echo '--- C: stdin between files'; node \"$B\" \"$T/bad2.jsonl\" - \"$T/good1.jsonl\" < \"$T/bad.jsonl\"; echo \"exit=$?\"; echo '--- D: two dashes'; node \"$B\" - - < \"$T/good1.jsonl\"; echo \"exit=$?\"; echo '--- E: two dashes with a file'; node \"$B\" \"$T/good1.jsonl\" - - < \"$T/good1.jsonl\"; echo \"exit=$?\"\nPASS: A prints `-:2: <error>` and `-:4: <error>` and exit=1; B prints nothing on stdout and exit=0; C prints `$T/bad2.jsonl:1: ...` then `-:2: ...` and `-:4: ...` and exit=1; D and E each print a message on stderr and exit=2. FAIL: stdin not read (e.g. `cannot read -`), prefix other than `-` for stdin rows, or D/E not exiting 2.\n\nCheck 3 — expect: \"Exit 0 if every file is clean, 1 if any row in any file is bad, 2 if no file is named or any file can't be read (error on stderr, other files still checked and reported)\"\nRun:\nT=$(mktemp -d) && printf '{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b\":2}\\n' > \"$T/good1.jsonl\" && printf '[1]\\n' > \"$T/good2.jsonl\" && printf '{\"a\":1}\\n{oops}\\n\\n{\"c\":\\n' > \"$T/bad.jsonl\" && printf '{bad\\n' > \"$T/bad2.jsonl\" && B=packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js && echo '--- A: two clean'; node \"$B\" \"$T/good1.jsonl\" \"$T/good2.jsonl\"; echo \"exit=$?\"; echo '--- B: one bad among clean'; node \"$B\" \"$T/good1.jsonl\" \"$T/bad2.jsonl\" \"$T/good2.jsonl\"; echo \"exit=$?\"; echo '--- C: no args'; node \"$B\"; echo \"exit=$?\"; echo '--- D: missing first, then bad and clean'; node \"$B\" \"$T/missing.jsonl\" \"$T/bad.jsonl\" \"$T/good1.jsonl\" 2> \"$T/err\"; echo \"exit=$?\"; echo \"stderr: $(cat \"$T/err\")\"; echo '--- E: missing among clean'; node \"$B\" \"$T/good1.jsonl\" \"$T/missing.jsonl\" \"$T/good2.jsonl\"; echo \"exit=$?\"\nPASS: A no output, exit=0; B prints only `$T/bad2.jsonl:1: ...`, exit=1; C a message on stderr, exit=2; D stdout still shows `$T/bad.jsonl:2: ...` and `$T/bad.jsonl:4: ...`, the stderr line names missing.jsonl, exit=2; E stderr names missing.jsonl, exit=2. FAIL: any other exit code, an unreadable file not reported on stderr, or later files not checked after the missing one (no bad.jsonl lines in D).\n\nCheck 4 — expect: \"lint(text) in src/index.js is unchanged\"\nRun:\nsha256sum packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js; git diff --exit-code b74bddb3b7f22287c00594ba1a9561398b675121 HEAD -- packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js && echo UNCHANGED\nPASS: hash is 7d43ab5104585408da4f6c0c230613b849084cf3b738717b385123017529c1e8 and `UNCHANGED` is printed. FAIL: different hash or a diff is shown.\n\nCheck 5 — expect: \"node:test tests cover two clean files, one bad among several, stdin via - (clean and bad), a missing file among good ones, two - arguments and no arguments; the package README documents the usage\"\nRun:\nnpm test 2>&1 | tail -12\nthen read the test files under packages/jsonl-lint/test/ and run:\ngrep -n -e '\\[<file>' -e 'stdin' packages/jsonl-lint/README.md\nPASS: npm test shows `# fail 0`; the node:test tests (spawning the bin) include a test for each of: two clean files, one bad file among several, `-` with clean stdin, `-` with bad stdin, a missing file among good ones, two `-` arguments, no arguments; and the README shows the multi-file usage (`<file> [<file> ...]`) and says `-` reads stdin. FAIL: any of the seven cases has no test, a test fails, or the README does not document multi-file / `-` usage.\n\nCheck 6 — expect: \"The change is one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body says Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/104, and npm test and the test workflow are green at its head\"\nRun:\ngh api 'repos/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/pulls?state=all&per_page=100' --jq '.[] | select((.body // \"\") | contains(\"Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/104\")) | \"\\(.number) \\(.state) \\(.head.sha) \\(.base.ref)\"'\nthen, with <sha> the head sha it printed:\ngh api 'repos/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/commits/<sha>/check-runs' --jq '.check_runs[] | \"\\(.name) \\(.status) \\(.conclusion)\"'\nand `npm test` at that head.\nPASS: exactly one open PR is listed, its head sha is the commit you are checking, the